# take(Function)
# The text of the program names the evaluator and hands it on: whoever gets it may give it any text, so the image admits code that nobody has read.
# It is the control of Bun's test/aot/engine-tests/image/holder-that-the-library-lets-go-hands-out-no-evaluator.ir and Bun's test/aot/engine-tests/image/name-read-off-a-value-nobody-knows-finds-no-evaluator.ir: what those two withhold is withheld from the lookups of the library and from whoever merely holds the holder.
# OPTIONS: exclude=CodeOutsideImage
# RUN: image
# CHECK: flags {{*}}AdmitsUnknownJavaScript

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=Function
    v1 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v2 = PropGet v1 key="take" [isFreeName]
    v3 = Call v2, -, v0 calleeName="take"
    v4 = Undefined
    Return v4
}
